      "nets": ["LED1"],
      "observed": "Net 'LED1' contains the 3.3V rail (L2.2, IC1.C1, C13.1, Q2.2, R2.2, U4.2, U5.28, U5.29) and also U5.34 (P1_LED) and U4.24 (LEDA_3_4).",
      "expected": "The +3V3 rail should be a separate net from the LED1 control net. U5.34 (P1_LED) is a GPIO and should not be tied to 3.3V; per spec, +3V3 destinations are U5.28, U5.29, U4.2, J2.4, R2, Q2 source.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"21\") (name \"LED1\") ... (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"34\") (pinfunction \"P1_LED\") (pintype \"bidirectional\")) ... (node (ref \"L2\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")) ..."
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "**`+3V3` rail destinations:** SKW92A module power pins (`U5.28`, `U5.29` — matching the datasheet's two dedicated `3.3VD` pins), keyboard `U4.2`, microSD `J2.4`, the gate pull-up `R2` (10 kΩ, pulling Q2's gate high/off by default), and the EPD power-switch MOSFET `Q2`'s source."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "U5.34 is forced to 3.3V, so it cannot be used as a GPIO to control the keyboard backlight anode. If configured as an output low, it will short 3.3V to ground, potentially damaging the pin or regulator. The backlight anode is always powered.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "C11 pin 1 is on net 'unconnected-(C11-Pad1)' with no other connections; pin 2 is on GND.",
      "expected": "A decoupling capacitor should be connected between a power rail and ground. C11 should have its pin 1 connected to a supply rail (e.g., +3V3 or BAT+).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"58\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"13\") (name \"GND\") ... (node (ref \"C11\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "C11 provides no decoupling; it is a floating capacitor. If it was intended to decouple a rail, that rail lacks the intended capacitance.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    },
    {
      "category": "footprint_mismatch",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": [],
      "nets": [],
      "observed": "C11 is a capacitor (libsource Device:C, value 0.1uF) but its footprint is 'Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder', an inductor footprint.",
      "expected": "A capacitor should use a capacitor footprint, e.g., 'Capacitor_SMD:C_0805_2012Metric...'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\") ... (libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C\") (description \"Unpolarized capacitor\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The component may not fit the intended pads, or the pads may be sized for an inductor, causing assembly issues. Since C11 is also unconnected, the immediate electrical impact is limited, but it indicates a design error.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a bridged net where the 3.3V rail is shorted to the LED1 control net (including U5.34 P1_LED), plus an unconnected capacitor C11 with an incorrect inductor footprint. These deviations would prevent proper keyboard backlight control and indicate assembly/connectivity errors."
}

